  ● ascend-cluster-fast-slow-rank-detector: Diagnoses fast/slow ranks in Ascend multi-card clusters using msprof-analyze and expert rules to identify           
    performance bottlenecks from computation, communication, or Host dispatch issues. It performs both macro-level qualitative analysis and micro-level root    
    cause drill-down for slow cards.                                                                                                                            

    ascend-communication-analysis: Analyzes Ascend NPU collective communication cost from profiling databases, separating wait-caused high duration from real   
    communication bottlenecks. Uses a DB-first workflow prioritizing cluster_analysis.db, analysis.db, and ascend_pytorch_profiler.db to diagnose HCCL/hcom     
    operations.                                                                                                                                                 

    ascend-computation-analysis: Diagnoses Ascend NPU computation-side performance problems including AI Core/Vector/AICPU hotspots, dynamic shape overhead,    
    fusion opportunities, and data movement issues. Designed for single-card or selected-rank analysis using profiling evidence to produce prioritized          
    optimization directions.                                                                                                                                    

    ascend-msprof-analyze-cli: Guides the use of msprof-analyze for comprehensive AI training/inference performance analysis, offering two modes: cluster       
    analysis (for large-scale multi-card scenarios with DB inputs) and advisor (for text/DB inputs with operator optimization suggestions). Selects the         
    appropriate mode based on data format, scale, and analysis requirements.                                                                                    

    ascend-npu-snapshot-analyzer: Analyzes PyTorch memory snapshot pickle files from _dump_snapshot() to detect memory peaks, fragmentation, leaks, and OOM     
    conditions with interactive HTML reports. Converts pickle data to SQLite DB and uses SQL macros for multi-dimensional memory analysis across 80% of common  
    scenarios.                                                                                                                                                  

    ascend-profiler-data-validation: Validates MindStudio profiler data integrity before in-depth analysis by checking data type identification, collection     
    completion status, key deliverables existence, and profiler configuration. Ensures framework profiler (PyTorch/MindSpore) and msprof data are correctly     
    parsed and ready for downstream analysis tools.                                                                                                             

    ascend-profiler-db-explorer: Translates natural language questions about Ascend Profiling databases (ascend_pytorch_profiler*.db, msprof_*.db) into safe,   
    executable SQL queries. Uses predefined CTE macros and dictionary rules for analyzing operator duration, communication time, dispatch, and scheduling from  
    profiling databases.                                                                                                                                        

    ascend-schedule-analysis: Analyzes NPU scheduling and Host Bound issues by examining device Free time, dispatch latency, launch gaps, and CPU runtime       
    interference. Prioritizes evidence-based investigation over tuning suggestions and requires device starvation evidence (Free time > 10%) before concluding  
    Host Bound.                                                                                                                                                 

    ascendc-operator-performance-optim: Provides end-to-end Ascend NPU operator performance tuning using msprof op, covering the full cycle from compilation,   
    performance collection, bottleneck analysis, code optimization, to before/after comparison reports. Works exclusively with operator source code directories 
    in a complete tuning pipeline.                                                                                                                              

    deterministic-calculation-analysis: Uses msProbe to compare dump data and identify the first API where inputs match but outputs differ in deterministic     
    computation. Supports three input types (dump paths, db, csv/xlsx) and allows excluding specific APIs to filter false positives.                            

    document-ux-review: Walks through a project's README, installation docs, and quick start as a first-time user to identify onboarding blockers and usability 
    issues. Produces actionable improvement recommendations based on real execution rather than superficial reading.                                            

    gen-evaluation-cfg: Generates single-file evaluation YAML configurations for msmodelslim's quant-tuning-evaluate/run_evaluation.py, containing demand,      
    evaluation (AISBench), and inference_engine (vLLM-Ascend) modules. Designed specifically for evaluation config generation, not practice/policy YAML.        

    gitcode-code-reviewer: Reviews GitCode PRs by combining PR metadata, diff, and full repository context to produce deep review conclusions or inline         
    comments. Requires a GitCode access token and analyzes changes beyond just the diff, including call chains, adjacent modules, and test coverage.            

    github-raw-fetch: Converts GitHub file page links to raw.githubusercontent.com URLs and fetches content via curl, with special handling for repository docs 
    routing via agent_router.md. Supports reading READMEs, source code, configuration, and documentation from GitHub repositories.                              

    mindstudio-cpu-binding: Diagnoses Host CPU affinity, NUMA locality, and cgroup/cpuset issues for NPU + PyTorch / LLM Serving workloads including vLLM-Ascend
    and SGLang. Produces evidence-based reports with conservative and advanced optimization recommendations, rollback plans, and before/after validation.       

    msmodeling-device-config: Guides users to convert natural language hardware descriptions into runnable DeviceProfile entries for unsupported accelerators,  
    GPUs, or NPUs. Uses a two-stage approach building a minimal runnable profile from confirmed facts and marking uncertain fields for later calibration.       

    msmodeling-env-installer: Installs and verifies the msmodeling development environment using uv, including requirements.txt installation, PYTHONPATH        
    configuration, and HF_ENDPOINT setup. Only activates when the user explicitly mentions msmodeling environment setup.                                        

    msmodeling-text-generate-executor: Interactively gathers parameters for the text_generate simulation command, explains assumptions, asks for confirmation,  
    then runs and summarizes performance metrics. Supports validating specific models, hardware profiles, and parallel strategies with progressive dialog.      

    msmodeling-throughput-optimizer-executor: Interactively gathers parameters for the throughput_optimizer deployment simulation, runs it, and summarizes the  
    best parallel strategy with concurrency, throughput, TTFT, and TPOT results. Compares hardware targets, aggregation vs disaggregation, and TP/EP/MOE-DP     
    search ranges.                                                                                                                                              

    msmodelslim-adapter-verification: Performs four-step functional validation for msModelSlim adapters after development, covering test model generation, full 
    fallback quantization, weight consistency checking, and actual quantization rule verification. Stops immediately on any failure with reasons and fix        
    suggestions.                                                                                                                                                

    msmodelslim-layer-wise-quantization: Implements layer-wise (lazy-loading) quantization for large models to reduce CPU memory peaks when full weight loading 
    is infeasible. An advanced optional feature activated only when the user explicitly requests it or when memory constraints prevent standard loading.        

    msmodelslim-model-adapt: Creates base Transformers model adapters for msModelSlim to enable W8A8/W4A16 quantization flows, supporting Decoder-only LLMs and 
    understanding VLMs (text backbone only). Covers adapter creation, required interface implementation, and registration/installation.                         

    msmodelslim-model-analysis: Analyzes candidate models before adapter implementation by determining implementation source, structural features, memory       
    constraints, and MoE fused weight risks. Supports Decoder-only LLMs and VLM text backbones, requiring config.json and modeling_*.py files.                  

    msmodelslim-model-dequant: Injects dequantization capability for FP8 quantized weights (per-block and per-channel) into the msModelSlim adapter workflow,   
    converting them to bf16/fp16 for further processing. Only supports FP8 formats with known dequantization rules; blocks on custom or non-FP8 formats.        

    msmodelslim-quick-quant: Provides quick quantization guidance for msModelSlim covering installation, minimal YAML configuration, and basic execution        
    verification. Uses placeholder-based paths and only covers linear_quant basics, excluding complex multi-stage flows or MoE mixed strategies.                

    msot-msopprof-operator-profiler: Analyzes Ascend AI operator performance using msOpProf (msprof op/simulator) for on-device or simulation tuning,           
    interpreting aic-metrics, trace.json, and visualize_data.bin outputs. Generates fixed analysis reports with operator basics, top-5 bottlenecks, and         
    optimization suggestions.                                                                                                                                   

    nan-overflow-detection: Detects NaN/Inf overflow in multi-card distributed training using MSProbe dump data by first locating the source rank where NaN     
    first appears, then tracing back to the root cause operator. Operates in two phases: cross-rank source detection followed by single-card root cause tracing.

    op-mfu-calculator: Calculates operator MFU (Machine FLOP Utilization) for matmul/GEMM operations given operator dimensions, runtime, and hardware peak      
    compute capability. Provides clear formulas, derivation steps, and reference peak FLOPs values for chips like Ascend 910B.                                  

    quant-tuning-evaluate: Evaluates quantized models by running scripts/run_evaluation.py according to an Evaluation YAML configuration. Focuses solely on the 
    evaluation step in the quantization tuning workflow.                                                                                                        

    quant-tuning-quantize: Executes model quantization by running msmodelslim quant according to a Practice YAML configuration. Focuses solely on the           
    quantization execution step in the tuning workflow.                                                                                                         

    quantization-accuracy-tuning-orchestrator: Provides end-to-end automated model quantization and accuracy tuning workflow using msmodelslim. Handles the     
    complete cycle including sensitive layer analysis, strategy decisions, quantization execution, and accuracy evaluation for precision recovery.              

    rl-consistency-analysis: Performs end-to-end root cause analysis for training/inference data inconsistencies by module mapping, value comparison, and       
    tracing the first divergence boundary. Filters fused or structural false positives along the producer-consumer chain and generates structured root cause    
    reports.                                                                                                                                                    

    tune-practice-cfg: Generates or modifies Practice YAML configurations for each round of quantization tuning, using sensitive layer analysis and previous    
    evaluation results to inform strategy decisions. Ensures the YAML passes validation before being passed to the quantizer for execution.                     

